 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "Tables II and III describe two individual patients with heterozygous TNFAIP3 variants, e.g. \"| S027 | TNFAIP3 | c.1127delC, p.S376fs\".",
 "method_note": "Cohort study of 123 FOXP3-negative IPEX-like patients; only the two TNFAIP3 carriers (S027, S087; Tables II and III) are in scope; the other 121 get no rows. JSON built by a short script from my own reading; every value checked against the tables by hand. Table II 'Age' column is not defined by the paper (it is not onset: S175 is '9 y' with 'Onset 3y'); recorded as age at last evaluation/time of report, uncertain (could be age at referral). Table II 'Inh' column is inheritance of the phenotype (AD), not variant origin, so variant inheritance is not reported; no parental testing is reported for these two. Genomic positions are from the column headed 'hg19 position'. Pathogenicity is the 'This study' column (P / LP, legend 'P: pathogenic; LP: likely pathogenic'); ClinVar column 'ni'. Column 'Functional consequence of mutation; evidence for causality' gives reasoning, not an assay result, so functional_evidence_statement is not reported. Variant type for S027 recorded as 'other' from 'LoF' / 'Truncating mutation' (no enum match); S087 type not stated (PPH2/gerp scores only). is_proband taken from the Discussion statement that only probands were available for initial analysis (cohort-wide). n_patients_reported left null: the paper never states the number of TNFAIP3 patients in words (two rows in Tables II and III). S087's only clinical feature is the label '“IPEX”', recorded as disease label; all S087 checklist items not reported. Eczema counted as observed for the composite skin-lesions checklist item; 'without frank thyroiditis' excludes autoimmune thyroiditis. No contradictions found. No stacked cells.",
